 - Bash: node "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --since 2026-03-29 --until 2026-04-12 --merge-identities | head -12; echo ---; git log --no-merges --since=2026-03-29 --until=2026-04-12 --format='%h %ad %an <%ae> | %s' --date=short; echo ---; git show --stat 62628c0 | tail -3
 - Bash: node "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --since 2026-03-29 --until 2026-04-12 --merge-identities --top 60 | grep -Ei 'vansh|fiona|troy|douglas'; echo ---; git show --stat 5317ebe | tail -4; git log -1 --format='%h %an' 5317ebe
FINAL ANSWER:
**Window:** 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12 (14 days up to the latest commit, 62628c0 on 2026-04-12). Lines are for the current ref (HEAD); commits are counted only in the window.

| Person | Commits in window | Surviving lines (share of 1,662 non-blank) |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 2 (`b2005d9`, `02afce3`, both 2026-04-10) | 649 (39.0%); 810 (40.8%) with blank lines |
| Vansh Sharma | 1 (`5317ebe`, 2026-04-07, docs) | 1 (0.1%) |
| Fiona Formatter | 1 (`62628c0`, 2026-04-12, reformat) | 0 in the table. The commit is set aside (below). |

People who committed in the window: Troy Goode, Vansh Sharma, and Fiona Formatter. Fiona's commit is not counted in the commit column.

**Troy Goode:** The 649 lines combine two addresses. The tool's guess is `<email redacted>` (605 lines, 0 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (44 lines, 2 commits). The name match is a guess from names and addresses, and the output does not give a strength label. Unmerged, the figures are 605 and 44. I could not confirm the identity from the output alone.

**Set-aside commit:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") by Fiona Formatter rewrote 291 lines. The tool treats it as a formatting-only commit and leaves it out of the table. Without that correction, the figures would be Troy 554 (33.3%), Douglas Christopher Wilson 376 (22.6%), and Fiona 291 (17.5%). I did not confirm the commit with `git show --stat` beyond its line count.

**Other notes from the output:**
- Douglas Christopher Wilson holds 551 lines (33.2%) but made no commit in the window. His last commit was in 2021.
- Bus factor (whole repository, `-C` copy detection): 2 (Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together hold 72.2%). It takes 4 authors to reach 80%. Without the reformat correction, the bus factor is still 2.
- Bots excluded: dependabot[bot], 10 lines.
- Five mechanical-looking commits were not set aside: `739dc11`, `fcd2b56`, `00d6eec`, `344ce1e`, and `9c2b59d`. None is in the window.
- One address with two names: Alejandro Caravaca Puchades and `alex94puchades` share `<email redacted>` (30 lines). They are not in the window.
- Copy detection: default `-C` figures. The output does not name anyone as moved by more than 2 points.
- Left out: lockfiles and generated files were not reported as dropped in this output.
- Prompt caveat: the tool's header reports 1,995 lines with blank lines, but its bus factor line reports 1,985. I used the header figure for the blank-line share.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git log -1 --format='%H %ad' --date=iso && git log --all --since='2026-03-25' --until='2026-04-13' --no-merges --format='%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s' --date=short && echo --- && git shortlog -sne --all | head -50
 - Bash: git log --all --since='2026-03-20' --until='2026-04-20' --format='%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s' --date=short && echo --- && git log --all --format='%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s' --date=short -n 3 && echo --- && cat .mailmap 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo; git show --stat --format='%h %an' b2005d9 02afce3 5317ebe 62628c0 | head -60
 - Bash: echo "$(git rev-parse 62628c0)" > /tmp/ignore-rev.txt && for mode in plain ignore; do echo "== $mode"; files=$(git ls-files | grep -E '\.(js|md|json|ts|yml|yaml|txt)$|^[^.]*$' ); if [ $mode = plain ]; then opt=""; else opt="--ignore-rev $(cat /tmp/ignore-rev.txt)"; fi; for f in $files; do [ -f "$f" ] && git blame --line-porcelain $opt HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^author ' ; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -15; done; echo; git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- lib/index.js | grep '^author-mail' | sort | uniq -c
 - Bash: IGN=$(git rev-parse 62628c0); for opt in "" "--ignore-rev $IGN"; do echo "== ${opt:-plain}"; git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do git blame --line-porcelain $opt HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^author-mail '; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -12; done; echo; git ls-files | wc -l
 - Bash: git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 HEAD -- lib/index.js | head -3; echo "rc=$?"; git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^author-mail '; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | grep -iE 'vansh|s.vansh|troy|fiona'; echo ---; git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do git blame --line-porcelain --ignore-rev 62628c0 HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^author-mail '; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -12
 - Bash: git show -w --stat --format='%h' b2005d9 | tail -2; git show -w b2005d9 | head -30
FINAL ANSWER:
**Window:** 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12 (14 days ending at the latest commit, 62628c0). Only four non-merge commits fall in it. Three people remain after excluding the formatting commit.

**1. Vansh Sharma** (<email redacted>)
- Commits in window:
  - `5317ebe` docs: app.del() with app.delete() in README example (#411), 2026-04-07
- Lines still in code today: **1** (the README line)

**2. Troy Goode** (<email redacted> and troy@laptop.example, counted as one person)
- Commits in window:
  - `02afce3` test: vary header coverage, 2026-04-10 (+36 lines)
  - `b2005d9` lib: annotate handlers, 2026-04-10 (12 lines changed; the `// checked` annotations are real edits, not whitespace, so this commit counts)
- Lines still in code today: **642** with formatting commit `62628c0` ignored, which attributes lines back to their real authors. Without that adjustment, `git blame` shows **261**, because Fiona's reformat claimed 1,016 lines.

**Excluded**
- `62628c0` style: reformat js, by Fiona Formatter (fiona@formatter.example). Formatting-only, so set aside as requested. This also means Fiona's raw line count (1,016) is not reported.
- Bots: none in the window (dependabot's commits are all older).

**Method:** `git log` for the window, then `git blame` across all 18 tracked files at HEAD, once plain and once with `--ignore-rev 62628c0`. The 642 figure is an approximation. Lines whose text changed in the reformat can't be traced back, so some of Troy's lines may still be credited elsewhere.
